    type: "input",
    question: "Una linea trifase ha tre conduttori con resistenza r = 2 Ω ciascuno e trasporta una corrente di linea I_l = 10 A. Calcola le perdite Joule complessive sui tre cavi P_persa = 3 · r · I_l² in Watt.",
    circuitSvg: "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 400 220\" class=\"circuit-diagram\">\n  <defs>\n    <pattern id=\"grid_89587\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" patternUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\">\n      <circle cx=\"2\" cy=\"2\" r=\"1\" fill=\"#334155\" />\n    </pattern>\n  </defs>\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"220\" fill=\"#0f172a\" rx=\"8\" />\n  \n      \n    <path d=\"M 120 50 L 126 40 L 138 60 L 150 40 L 162 60 L 174 40 L 180 50\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" />\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"32\" fill=\"#fde047\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">r = 2 Ω</text>\n  \n      \n    <path d=\"M 120 100 L 126 90 L 138 110 L 150 90 L 162 110 L 174 90 L 180 100\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" />\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"82\" fill=\"#fde047\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">r = 2 Ω</text>\n  \n      \n    <path d=\"M 120 150 L 126 140 L 138 160 L 150 140 L 162 160 L 174 140 L 180 150\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" />\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"132\" fill=\"#fde047\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">r = 2 Ω</text>\n  \n      <text x=\"50\" y=\"55\" fill=\"#f87171\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\">L₁</text>\n      <text x=\"50\" y=\"105\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\">L₂</text>\n      <text x=\"50\" y=\"155\" fill=\"#34d399\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\">L₃</text>\n      <text x=\"260\" y=\"105\" fill=\"#fde047\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\">I_l = 10 A</text>\n    \n</svg>",
    correctAnswer: 600,
    unit: "W",
    explanation: "\n      <strong>💡 Trucco mentale per la palestra:</strong><br>\n      • Perdita per singolo conduttore: <code>r × I² = 2 × 10² = 2 × 100 = 200 W</code>.<br>\n      • Sui tre conduttori di linea: <code>3 × 200 W = 600 W</code>!\n    "
